WEBVTT

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.740
Matsuo.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:15.240
Come with me.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.500
Let me be direct with you.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.760
You've been slacking off, haven't you?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.770
Everyone <i>knows</i> you've been slacking!

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.900
Matsuo, you haven't been practicing
as hard as you could have.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.660
In yesterday's game, the second 
you didn't have to play anymore...

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.410
when you were being 
subbed out, you smiled!

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.790
Yeah, I have been slacking off.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.540
Why won't you take this seriously?!

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.550
You'd better have a good reason!

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.640
Not really.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.880
You bastard!

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.010
Even if I did explain, 
I doubt you'd understand.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:23.890
Explain yourself!

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.150
Okay, then, let me ask you something.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:39.400
How many of you are 100% certain 
we'll make it to Hanazono?

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.470
I mean, I get that you're working hard 
because you believe we <i>could </i>get there.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.930
But you all know that's not what I'm asking.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.040
In the three months since Komori-san
showed up, we've gotten stronger, sure...

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.810
But do you really think we can beat Ryoin,
who've ruled our region 15 years in a row?

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:22.950
I mean, I think we can get there eventually.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:27.350
The second-years seem motivated,
and we have some experienced first-years.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.960
But I'm sorry. I think it's too late for me.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.130
What does that have to do with 
you half-assing practice?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.850
Kashi.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.040
They're unrelated.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.850
You're saying you've been slacking off 
because you don't think we can win this year?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.190
Why doesn't watching your juniors work hard
 pressure you into keeping up with them?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.750
You always said you wanted 
to follow Sekizan's example.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:11.750
Sorry.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.870
I'm thirsty. I'm getting a drink.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.400
Toshi!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:27.170
You said we'd go to the same college 
and keep playing rugby together!

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.640
What are you going to do 
if you don't get better?

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.250
Sorry. I didn't tell you.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.790
I can't go to college anymore.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.700
Sorry.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.070
In a few months, I'll be done with rugby.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.740
So please don't waste time
worrying about me.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:02.930
Spend the time on the youngsters instead.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.750
I'd rather you play the talented Oharano
instead of me.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:18.770
If he plays in a lot of games this year, 
they might be able to win next year.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.460
Do you seriously think that?

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:26.790
Were you lying when you said 
you wanted to be like Sekizan?

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.950
Were those two and a half 
years of effort all a lie?

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.750
I still...

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.200
want to be like Taku.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.430
But I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.120
No matter what anyone says...

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.800
I can't take it seriously.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.980
If saying I wanted to be like Taku made
 it so, we wouldn't be in this situation.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:09.910
Sorry.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:59.500
<b>Episode 24 
The Opponent We Never 
Could've Fought</b>

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.220
Crouch. Bind.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.080
Set.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.490
Oharano!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.440
Got it.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.460
I could kick the ball, but...

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.540
Kibi-senpai!

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:23.170
What?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.690
Let's see what you can do one more time.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.920
Kick it! Kick it as hard as you can!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.020
I-It's out! It's gone into touch!

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.280
All right, okay!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.330
Kibi-kun, nice kick!

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:53.830
That was good.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.990
Don't surprise me like that, Oharano.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:01.000
You're a lot stronger than I am.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.930
Your control isn't the best at times, though.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.010
I'll work on it.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:16.300
<i>Here it comes.</i>

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.040
What?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.490
I-It was a fake out?

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.690
You fell for it.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.110
Don't let me fall!

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.540
Kasshi, nice!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.000
Dammit.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.540
Get it back!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.890
Pass the ball!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.630
I'll keep the ball moving!

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.170
Ryoin's fast!

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.180
Jinko's passing just isn't quick enough.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.930
Dammit. Fine, then.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.860
He threaded his way through the forwards!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.750
Go!

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.360
Oharano!

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.320
You definitely...

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:19.310
You definitely won't get past me!

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:21.330
I'll flip you over!

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.080
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:33.990
<i>I'm counting on you...</i>

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.460
<i>Suwa-san.</i>

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.680
Suwa!

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.780
He got past him!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.440
Suwa!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.070
Go!

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.930
Score a try, Suwa!

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.920
Nice try.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:26.930
We underestimated them.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.050
Coach...

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:33.170
I'll have to chew them out later.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.010
<b>Aaah!</b>

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.010
<b>Aaah!</b>

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.990
<b>Aaah!</b>

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.990
Smiling

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:40.990
Oh...

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:42.910
This is amazing!

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.990
We scored first against Ryoin!

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.760
Suwawesome!

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.390
That was a pretty decent try.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:51.870
You...

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.230
You're in the way.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.500
I'll take the conversion. Move already.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.640
<b>Oh...</b>

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:01.640
Don't worry about it.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.760
Shut up! You should've scored 
closer to center field!

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.730
Kifune, you might've made that kick.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.020
Th-That's not true.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.070
Jinko could win this.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:15.270
You can do it!

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:25.270
Hey, Sekki...

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:34.800
I don't like how
everyone's really mad at Mattsu.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.190
I've always played scrum-half.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:47.420
Since Mattsu started playing fly-half, 
you'd get the ball out of the scrum,

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:49.380
I'd grab the ball...

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.230
and pass it to Mattsu.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:57.000
He sucked at first.

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.070
Our coordination was terrible.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.680
We practiced over and over.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:06.490
Now he's always standing exactly 
where I want him to be.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.990
Something must've happened.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:18.780
I would've noticed otherwise.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:24.890
We fought all the time as first-years 
and then, as second-years.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.070
We've fought enough.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:36.150
Let's beat Ryoin in this game
and open his eyes.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.540
Matsuo!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.070
You need to get it into your head already.

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:58.270
Our opponents are really close to us, 
so you need to be standing closer.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.800
S-Sorry.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.080
Hey, Kamo...

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:05.850
Don't be so hard on the beginners 
just because you've played before.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.790
Right, Matsuo?

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:12.080
Besides, this is how we play, right?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:16.060
This isn't your middle school.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.490
You're insolent.

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:24.880
Let's put Sekizan in
the starting lineup next time.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.080
He sucks, but he's huge.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:31.080
And no matter what we make 
him do, he never complains.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:36.290
Let's start from a scrum again!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.460
Raita.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.550
I'll pay more attention to 
where our opponents are.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:49.110
Sorry.

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.990
<i>Even though he sucked,</i>

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.530
<i>the one thing he was good at was 
getting along with the upperclassmen.</i>

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.320
<i>But he wasn't a bad guy.</i>

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:06.100
<i>I didn't like him enough 
to protect him, though.</i>

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:07.760
Raita!

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.910
A-An interception!

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:15.910
He's fast...

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.820
Raita, why were you just standing there?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.040
Dammit.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.210
This isn't good!

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.620
Jinko!

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.920
Matsu-san, cheer with us!

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.180
Gion, stop him!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.370
Sekki!

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:00.880
Get up, idiot!

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.000
Captain, nice tackle!

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.380
He's unbelievable.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.760
That's their captain, Sekizan.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.550
I'm surprised he took down both of them.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:31.780
Ryoin

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:31.780
Jinko

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.630
Captain!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.780
Jinko, win the ball back!

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:38.580
We keep making tackles...

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.290
...but we can't get the ball.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.840
Jinko's individuals aren't playing badly,

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:50.210
but their reckless overall game shows
they're not thinking about the next play.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:55.930
They have the basics down, 
but not the application.

00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:02.190
But don't you think Jinko's giving our 
second string a little <i>too </i>much trouble?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.690
I won't deny that.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.240
H-He lifted him off the ground!

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.400
Iwashi, keep going!

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.380
It's a maul!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.360
Get it out! Quickly!

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.430
Don't let go, Iwashi!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.390
Gotcha...

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.740
Pile-up!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:53.420
Since Ryoin didn't release the ball from
the maul, form another scrum, Jinko's ball.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.410
All right!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.660
All right! Scrum!

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.640
There's less than ten minutes left
in the first half.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:05.480
Things are going well.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:08.920
We're piling the pressure on to Ryoin.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.500
Crouch. Bind.

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.260
Set!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.930
<i>The game's not going too badly.</i>

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:29.810
<i>But the movements of some 
of our players isn't great.</i>

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:35.570
Put your backs into it, Ryoin!

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:44.290
They got it again!

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.080
All right!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.290
Shut up, Kokuto.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.950
What the heck are you doing, Shinshi?!

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.020
Sorry!

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.970
Argh, dammit!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.800
<i>The third-years...</i>

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:59.190
Focus!

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.500
Don't let them go any farther!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:04.560
<i>Crap! Crap!</i>

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:14.360
<i>The coach and Sekito-san will think
we're struggling against these weaklings.</i>

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.380
<i>Crap!</i>

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.210
<i>I need to impress them!</i>

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:19.320
Mikado!

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:31.050
Let go!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.750
Ryoin's failure to release the ball!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:37.570
What?

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:40.240
Mikado, you bastard!

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.550
You idiot!

00:18:58.750 --> 00:18:59.930
Sekizan.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.330
Stop looking off the field.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:12.960
I'm not saying I'm not 
worried about Matsuo...

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:16.650
And I'm not saying I want to abandon him...

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:19.190
But this...

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.720
But this is no time to be
 looking at the bench!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:28.730
Standing in front of us is an opponent 
we never could've fought before!

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.940
You said so yourself before the game!

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.480
S-Sorry.

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.610
Let's focus on the next play.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:53.370
I have an idea.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.730
Are you serious?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:57.810
Of course.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.650
That was a good kick.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.060
It's less than ten meters 
to Ryoin's goal line.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:07.830
Dammit.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:09.890
I won't let them through.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:15.650
Jinko's #8 is in the scrum-half's position.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.810
Which means they're going for a maul.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:27.680
It's a maul!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.200
Push them back!

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:32.100
Captain.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.130
I-It's not a maul?

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.120
Mutsumi.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.730
He peeled off.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:21.670
Try!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:23.970
All right!

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:27.080
Hachi, you did it!

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.540
Hachi-senpai!

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:29.140
We did it.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.190
Mutsumi.

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.430
Sekizan.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.010
Peeling off worked.

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:34.060
We did it!

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.350
Nice pass.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.560
We made the kick!

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:44.300
It's 12-0!

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:48.630
Th-This is amazing!

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.620
Jinko's on a roll!

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.750
You're finally awake, Ryujin?

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:04.460
I've been awake the whole time.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:05.380
Liar.

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:13.280
Hm?

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "All Out"</b>

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:48.690
Next time: "All Out!"
